{"uid":"38505f756115e83f","name":"test_steer_and_retry_proxies_forward_the_control_token_and_surface_a_401_reason","fullName":"tests.test_cli_ui#test_steer_and_retry_proxies_forward_the_control_token_and_surface_a_401_reason","historyId":"9396ccbcedd30130de0844c1fba2c2ff","time":{"start":1791969056224,"stop":1791969057198,"duration":974},"description":"#155: the hub's steering form (`POST /api/runs/<id>/steer`) and its\n    \"retry now\" button (`POST /api/runs/<id>/retry`) are the two mutating\n    proxies `_proxy_json` forwards to a run's live container API. A real\n    run's mutating routes gate on a SECOND, independent secret --\n    `X-Ralphd-Control-Token`, checked against `.control-token` -- which\n    `ralphctl start`/`resume` provisions unconditionally (see main.py's\n    `api()` helper forwarding the same header for the CLI's own mutating\n    commands). Before this fix `_proxy_json` forwarded only `.api-token`\n    (`Authorization`), so every hub-initiated steer/retry against a real\n    run 401'd.\n\n    Two things pinned in one node, both against the SAME engine double so\n    there is no room for the two proxies to drift out of sync with each\n    other: (1) the control token is present, unforged, on BOTH requests;\n    (2) when the engine refuses with the control-token gate's own 401 (the\n    literal shape `engine/api.py`'s `auth` middleware sends), the hub's JSON\n    answer still carries that reason rather than flattening it away -- the\n    same body shape `app.js`'s steer-form and retry-button failure branches\n    both parse (via the shared `innermostReason` helper, task 069) to\n    render it.","descriptionHtml":"<p>#155: the hub's steering form (<code>POST /api/runs/&lt;id&gt;/steer</code>) and its<br />\n&quot;retry now&quot; button (<code>POST /api/runs/&lt;id&gt;/retry</code>) are the two mutating<br />\nproxies <code>_proxy_json</code> forwards to a run's live container API. A real<br />\nrun's mutating routes gate on a SECOND, independent secret --<br />\n<code>X-Ralphd-Control-Token</code>, checked against <code>.control-token</code> -- which<br />\n<code>ralphctl start</code>/<code>resume</code> provisions unconditionally (see main.py's<br />\n<code>api()</code> helper forwarding the same header for the CLI's own mutating<br />\ncommands). Before this fix <code>_proxy_json</code> forwarded only <code>.api-token</code><br />\n(<code>Authorization</code>), so every hub-initiated steer/retry against a real<br />\nrun 401'd.</p>\n<pre><code>Two things pinned in one node, both against the SAME engine double so\nthere is no room for the two proxies to drift out of sync with each\nother: (1) the control token is present, unforged, on BOTH requests;\n(2) when the engine refuses with the control-token gate's own 401 (the\nliteral shape `engine/api.py`'s `auth` middleware sends), the hub's JSON\nanswer still carries that reason rather than flattening it away -- the\nsame body shape `app.js`'s steer-form and retry-button failure branches\nboth parse (via the shared `innermostReason` helper, task 069) to\nrender it.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791968776876,"stop":1791968776877,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791968776877,"stop":1791968776877,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791969056181,"stop":1791969056181,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasCo